{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization has all prerequisites met for this workflow. P-LIT-GHA-CACHE (dependency caching) is already implemented for NuGet with a lockfile-aware key, so an equivalent cache exists. P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (cancel remaining matrix jobs after failure) is GitHub Actions' default behavior, so no workflow change is needed. P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is contraindicated because this workflow performs release/upload work. P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE and P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE do not apply because the workflow is a reusable workflow_call with no scheduled triggers. P-LIT-BAZEL-* patterns do not apply because there is no Bazel build. P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT lacks its precondition: the only recorded CI run failed, so there is no representative successful-duration history from which to derive a timeout. The cloudtune scenario experiments (P-LIT-ENV-CACHE, P-LIT-BAZEL-DEPS, P-LIT-BAZEL-INCREMENTAL) target a different workflow/system (cloudtune-scenario.yml with CT_PATTERN/CT_POLICY/CT_DATA) and are not applicable to this artifacts.yml workflow. Applying any speculative change would risk weakening coverage or adding unrelated changes.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
